      "text": "**The north has better air right now.** The latest readings I found, at **11:00 a.m. Singapore time on October 17**, show 1-hour PM2.5 at **83 µg/m³ in the north** versus **158 µg/m³ in the west**. The 24-hour PSI was **139 north** and **176 west**. Both readings indicate unhealthy air, but the north is better on both measures. ([hazemonitor.com](https://hazemonitor.com/singapore/north))\n\nFor how the air is *right now*, the 1-hour PM2.5 comparison is more useful; the PSI reflects a longer period. The regional readings may differ from conditions at a specific address. ([hazemonitor.com](https://hazemonitor.com/singapore/north))",
